{
  "id": "EUVD-2026-129029",
  "enisaUuid": "8e3dc0e1-0e7b-3a53-afea-92835b235bde",
  "description": "A vulnerability in Object Linking and Embedding, 2nd Generation (OLE2) file parser for ClamAV could allow an unauthenticated, remote attacker to cause a DoS condition on an affected device.\r\n\r This vulnerability is due to logic error when parsing specifically formatted files with the OLE2 file parser. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by by sending a crafted Microsoft Compound File Binary (CFB) file to be scanned. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to allocate all available memory, causing the ClamAV scanning process to terminate, resulting in a DoS condition on the affected software.",
  "datePublished": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:31:54 PM",
  "dateUpdated": "Nov 18, 2026, 4:42:46 PM",
  "baseScore": 7.5,
  "baseScoreVersion": "3.1",
